    "notes": "CONTEXT-LENGTH SWEEP, pre-registered. Identical to go2_contact_40d in every respect except model.block_size. NeRD uses h=10 at 1/60 s (0.167 s); our 128 at 100 Hz is 1.28 s, 7.7x longer, and their curve is NON-MONOTONIC (h=5 worse than h=1 on Ant), so 128 cannot be defended by 'longer is safer'. HYPOTHESIS: 1.28 s of a periodic gait lets the model predict the next state from phase alone without attending to the action -- action-blindness. PRE-REGISTERED READING: gate corr at 0.5 s rising monotonically as context shrinks supports it; flat closes the line. One-step val_loss is expected to WORSEN as context shrinks; if val_loss and gate corr move the SAME way, the mechanism is wrong."
